<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Core-ancestor derivation and one-lookup guard for the invoice family</title>
    <phase>1 Data model (WP1)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes a shared security component (CoreAncestorResolver, its TypeScript mirror, SecureChildLineage) on the write path; tags security, write-path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive change to access derivation and secure-family registration with 7 dependencies and cross-project review (uac-r2); judgment on taxonomy boundaries.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>010, 012, 020, 021, 022, 023, 027</deps>
    <tags>bff, dataverse, write-path, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give the invoice family (sprk_invoice, sprk_billingevent, sprk_invoicesubmission, sprk_invoiceapproval, sprk_externalidentifier) one server-side owner for the FR-05 invariant: exactly one entity-specific core-record lookup (Matter, Project or Work Assignment) per record, all five resolver fields derived from it, and a write populating two refused fail-closed — built on CoreAncestorResolver. Register every new invoice-family table with the secure-record family so rows under a secure matter are Secure-team-owned, not ordinary-owned. Reviewed by unified-access-control-r2.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Spaarke access model (core ancestors, secure-child lineage), Dataverse write paths and fail-closed design.</role>

  <goal>A pure, unit-tested guard and derivation in Services/Dataverse that, given one of the five entities and its pending field values, returns the single core record and the five resolver-field values, or a refusal with a stable reason when zero or more than one entity-specific lookup is set; CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns and its TypeScript mirror read sprk_invoice's new sprk_regardingworkassignment; the new tables are registered consistently in the secure-family lists and carry sprk_createdbyperson where app-only-created; uac-r2's review is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Today sprk_invoice is a CHILD in the access taxonomy and an intermediate whose root columns are its typed sprk_project / sprk_matter (CoreAncestorResolver.cs:92-101, :182); an invoice naming both a matter and a project currently derives two stamps (DeriveStampsAsync :648-687) — FR-05 says a write populating two is refused. sprk_billingevent is in SecureChildLineage (SecureChildLineage.cs:74-75) with typed matter / project lookups, and sprk_invoice at :130-132. The C# tables are pinned to the TypeScript INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS / CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES in PolymorphicResolverService.ts by CoreAncestorResolverTests (IntermediateRootColumns_MatchTheTypeScriptSide). Naming scheme (coordinator decision): new tables 020 / 021 / 022 (and 023 / 027 if they carry core lookups) use the CoreAncestorLookups names sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingproject / sprk_regardingworkassignment (CoreAncestorResolver.cs:116-122); sprk_invoice and sprk_billingevent reuse their typed sprk_matter / sprk_project and gain sprk_regardingworkassignment (010 / 012) - this task maps each entity's three lookups for the guard. Secure family today: sprk_invoice and sprk_billingevent are already in config/secure-record-owner-role.json, SecureChildLineage, the census (RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs:47-48) and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables (line 157); SecureFamilyConsistencyTests fails unless lineage, role set and census agree (allow-lists empty). InvoiceReviewService.BuildInvoiceCreateFields (~line 828) is today's resolver-field write shape to copy.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts (INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS mirror only)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/__tests__/PolymorphicResolverService.coreAncestor.test.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.cs (pure guard + resolver-field derivation; final name may follow sibling conventions)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Dataverse/InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">config/secure-record-owner-role.json (tables[] kind child: new family tables)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (ChildTables)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/domain/Access/SecureChildLineageTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 ($Tables, line 157) and src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordCreatorPerson.cs (StampedChildTables, line 78 - same list)</file>
      <file role="read">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SecureFamilyConsistencyTests.cs (must pass unchanged; allow-lists stay empty)</file>
      <file role="read">scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 (run against dev after the config change)</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">sprk_billingevent sprk_regardingworkassignment + resolver fields</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">sprk_invoice sprk_regardingworkassignment</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">sprk_invoicesubmission core-record fields</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">sprk_invoiceapproval core-record fields</dependency>
      <dependency task="022" status="pending">sprk_externalidentifier core-record fields</dependency>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">sprk_billingexport table (secure-family registration)</dependency>
      <dependency task="027" status="pending">correction record shape (child table to register, or columns on the line - nothing to register)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-68 / task 022 (2026-10-15)">Define the sprk_regardingrecordid value for sprk_externalidentifier rows that belong to an invoice only (no core record yet), so the D-68 alternate key (firm, type, value, core record) never has an empty column; task 044 writes it. Rows with an empty key column escape the key and can duplicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-75">Per D-75 (with ontology-r1, 2026-10-15): the core record of an invoice line (sprk_billingevent) is derived only from the line's OWN core-record lookup (sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_regardingworkassignment, FR-05), never by walking sprk_billingevent.sprk_invoice; a line may in future not belong to exactly one invoice. Any other derivation needs uac-r2 approval (STOP and ask).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024 / spec FR-05">The guard refuses (does not pick one) when more than one of the entity's Matter / Project / Work Assignment lookups is set, and when none is set on an entity where FR-05 requires one; the refusal carries a stable reason code. When exactly one is set, it returns all five resolver fields (type via sprk_recordtype_ref, id lowercase "D" GUID, name, relative URL, number) — never a partial set.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034 / NFR-01 of the access model">Fail closed: a metadata or read failure is a refusal, never "no ancestor". Keep CoreAncestorStatus.NoAncestor and Error distinct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT add any new entity to ChildRecordEntities or CoreRecordEntities, and do not change StampSourceColumns or StampedOutsideAccessTaxonomy, without uac-r2's written agreement (escalation trigger). Adding sprk_regardingworkassignment to IntermediateRootColumns["sprk_invoice"] and its TypeScript mirror is in scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / uac-r2">Secure-record family registration: SecureChildLineage gets every core-record lookup on sprk_invoice and sprk_billingevent (an omitted lookup can widen a share intersection) and a lineage row for each new family table - sprk_invoicesubmission, sprk_invoiceapproval, sprk_externalidentifier, sprk_billingexport and the correction table (only if 027 chose a child table). The same tables go, in the same change, into config/secure-record-owner-role.json (kind child, privilegeName, reason, evidence, addedBy "ebilling-r1 task 013"), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.ChildTables and SecureChildLineageTests; SecureFamilyConsistencyTests passes with empty allow-lists. Tables created app-only (no human caller) also go into Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables and RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables. Every table entry is reviewed by uac-r2 before merge.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF change: state placement (in BFF, write-path owner), measure publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE, tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/. No DI registration is needed for a pure static guard; if one is added, it goes in the existing Dataverse registration (ADR-010).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests: unit tests for the guard (zero, one, two, three lookups; each core type; resolver fields complete) and the updated pinning tests. Seeding proof for the more-than-one refusal.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/dataverse/polymorphic-resolver.md</file>
