    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the dependency tasks' notes for exact lookup names; read CoreAncestorResolver, SecureChildLineage, the TS mirror and their pinning tests.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the guard tests first (fail before): two-lookup refusal per pair, zero-lookup refusal, one lookup per core type returning five complete resolver fields, unknown entity refused.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the guard as a pure component reusing CoreAncestorResolver's tables / record-type resolution; no Dataverse write in it.</step>
    <step order="4">Add sprk_regardingworkassignment to IntermediateRootColumns["sprk_invoice"] and the TS INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS; update the pinning tests on both sides.</step>
    <step order="5">Secure-family registration: list the family tables and, per table, whether it is created app-only (from 020-023 / 027 notes); present the list to uac-r2; on agreement update SecureChildLineage (lookups + rows), the role config, the census, SecureChildLineageTests, RecordCreatorPerson and the creator-person script together; run SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and the unit tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Run Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 against dev (-WhatIf first); record output. Record uac-r2's answers to the escalation questions; apply only what they agree.</step>
    <step order="7">Seeding proof: disable the more-than-one refusal, confirm the named test fails, restore; record.</step>
    <step order="8">dotnet build / dotnet test (unit + ArchTests) and the Spaarke.UI.Components jest suite for the touched test; measure publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to ✅ [done].</step>
    <step order="10">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Adding any table to the CHILD access taxonomy (ChildRecordEntities) is a uac-r2 / owner decision: STOP and ask. Secure-family registration is in scope, but if uac-r2 says a new table must NOT be Secure-team-owned, STOP and record the decision rather than allow-listing a gap.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the mixed naming (typed sprk_matter / sprk_project on invoice and line, sprk_regarding{core} elsewhere) cannot map cleanly in the guard or the resolver, STOP and decide with the owner and uac-r2 before any column is created or renamed.</trigger>
    <trigger>If refusing an existing invoice row with both sprk_matter and sprk_project set during derivation (not only at write) would change behaviour for existing data in dev, STOP and present the row count and options to uac-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CoreAncestorResolver derives stamps and refuses same-type conflicts (CoreAncestorResolver.cs:658-671) but has no write-time "exactly one core lookup" check; InvoiceReviewService.BuildInvoiceCreateFields writes resolver fields for a matter only. Grep for a one-lookup guard over Services/Dataverse finds none.</existing>
    <extension>Partly — tables and record-type resolution are reused from CoreAncestorResolver; the guard is a separate small pure component because CoreAncestorResolver derives from rows already written, while FR-05 must refuse before the write (ADR-002 single owner).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A write naming two core records is accepted, so access inheritance and the "line's core record is authoritative" rule become ambiguous; FR-05's negative acceptance ("a write populating two is refused") fails, and every invoice-family writer (044, 049, 100, 104) re-implements resolver-field logic.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Run the Spaarke.UI.Components test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs, PolymorphicResolverService.ts</output>
    <output type="config">config/secure-record-owner-role.json, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Dataverse/InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuardTests.cs, CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs, SecureChildLineageTests.cs, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs, PolymorphicResolverService.coreAncestor.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per D-75, CoreAncestorResolver derives a sprk_billingevent row's core record from its own core lookup: a test with a line whose sprk_invoice points at a different (or no) invoice still resolves the line's own matter / project / work assignment, and a line with no core lookup is refused, not resolved through the invoice.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For each of the five entities: given exactly one of Matter / Project / Work Assignment set, the guard returns that core record and five non-empty resolver fields; given two or three set, it returns a refusal with a stable reason code; given none, it returns a refusal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A read or metadata failure inside the derivation yields a refusal, not success and not "no ancestor".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">IntermediateRootColumns["sprk_invoice"] and the TypeScript mirror both include sprk_regardingworkassignment; the C#-to-TypeScript pinning tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureChildLineage includes every core-record lookup now on sprk_invoice and sprk_billingevent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each new family table (submission, approval, external identifier, export, correction table if one exists) appears in SecureChildLineage, config/secure-record-owner-role.json (kind child), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.ChildTables and SecureChildLineageTests; SecureFamilyConsistencyTests passes with all allow-lists empty; removing one table from one list makes it fail (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each app-only-created family table is in Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables and RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables; both dev scripts' output (role privileges, sprk_createdbyperson) is recorded; uac-r2 reviewed every table entry.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof recorded: with the more-than-one refusal disabled, the named guard test fails; restored, it passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ChildRecordEntities, CoreRecordEntities, StampSourceColumns and StampedOutsideAccessTaxonomy are unchanged unless uac-r2's written agreement is recorded in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">uac-r2 review recorded in task notes (FR-05 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE; dotnet build and all touched test suites pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Security tag: two adversarial-verifier passes (root CLAUDE.md §8.5). Callers (044 submission, 049 job, 100 review, 104 resubmission) call the guard before any invoice-family create / update; this task does not wire them. uac-r2 shares these files - run /conflict-check before the PR. Not parallel-safe: RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs is also edited by 011, and the secure-family files are uac-r2's. Deps 023 / 027 added beyond the brief (their tables need registration).

Completed 2026-10-15 (notes/013-core-ancestor-invoice-family.md). Guard + stored-row derivation built and tested; invoice WA root column in C#, TS and the container resolver (lockstep); submission, approval, external identifier and correction registered in the secure family (dev role applied and verified, 403 before / 201 after) and given sprk_createdbyperson (dev applied, -Verify PASS). Deviation: sprk_billingexport NOT registered (no root, spans many core records) - ISS-011 (#1974) for the owner / uac-r2. ISS-010 (#1973): the generic child-record create route bypasses the guard. uac-r2 review of the table entries is still outstanding. Rework: one review fix (the approval's Decision Record lineage edge was removed, F1). The invoice's sprk_supersedesinvoice lineage edge was removed after the full suite showed it altered the external invoices module's root rule; its classification is left to uac-r2. Full BFF suite: 23,346 passed. The 23 load-flaky WAF failures pass in isolation (146/146).</notes>

